  "knowledge": "PostgreSQL answers COMMIT with the command tag COMMIT, so the client knows that the transaction committed.",
  "api_outcome": {
    "reported": "committed",
    "basis": "pgx.Tx.Commit returned nil",
    "contract": "pgx v5.11.0 Tx.Commit (tx.go, dbTx.Commit) executes COMMIT and returns ErrTxCommitRollback when the command tag is ROLLBACK. The Tx interface documents that a commit which fails with a rollback status returns an error where errors.Is(ErrTxCommitRollback) is true. ErrTxCommitRollback's comment says PostgreSQL accepts COMMIT on an aborted transaction and treats it as ROLLBACK. A nil error is pgx's report that the transaction committed. dbTx.Rollback executes ROLLBACK and, on any error, calls Conn.die, which closes the connection. A nested Tx.Begin is a savepoint. Nested Rollback executes ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT and does not close the connection.",
    "error": null,
    "steps": {}
  },
